---
title: "On the existence of integrable Reeb flows"
speaker: "Jakob Hedicke (Radboud University, Nijmegen)"
date: 2026-06-03
time: 3-4 pm
room: BB 5161.0293
mathjax: true
abstract: >

  Bott-integrable Reeb flows on contact 3-manifolds are flows of a Reeb vector field that admit a Morse-Bott function invariant under the flow.

They naturally appear for example in the study of geodesics on surfaces or more generally of 4 dimensional Hamiltonian integrable systems.

In this talk we will discuss the (non-) existence and properties of such Reeb flows. In particular we will see that the existence of a Bott-integrable Reeb flow does not only impose strong restrictions on the topology of the manifold, but also on the underlying contact structure, i.e. the symplectic hyperplane bundle transverse to the Reeb vector field.

The talk is based on joint work with Hansjörg Geiges and Murat Sağlam.
